  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_intro",
      "text": "ENGINE ROOM HARNESS C - PARTIAL. Only new / upgraded / relocated feeds. Do not redraw the OEM engine-room, cowl or dash looms. Kick-panel J/B No.1, R/B No.2 / No.3 / No.4 stay. Unplug engine-bay J/B No.2 and F11; inject at the pins in the splice table (docs/electrical/ENGINE-ROOM-POWER-REDISTRIBUTION.md). J/B1 1H is not touched: 1H-7 IG2 (B-O from the ignition switch) stays, do not overlay; 1H-8 is on the always-hot bus.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_heavy",
      "text": "HEAVY DC: trunk battery -> cabin PDB (glove box) -> RADLOK 5.7 mm through the firewall -> starter B+. 160 A alt B+ joins the starter post and does not recross; its protection is NOT at the starter (see n_alt_prot). Jump lugs at trunk battery, PDB, starter, engine block, and the engine-bay jump post. 2 AWG is OK for cranking; 160 A continuous charge may need 1/0 + 8 mm RADLOK - see the table.",
      "color": "Orange",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 210
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_split",
      "text": "RED / BLUE PHYSICAL ROUTE (Daniel's marked-up path, 2026-09-29; corrected for J/B No.2's real side - see n_jb2_side below). RED (heavy DC): trunk battery -> up the passenger side of the cabin -> glove-box PDB -> through the passenger side into the engine bay -> RADLOK firewall pair -> alternator and starter. BLUE (normal power): from the passenger-side glove-box PDB / gbx_body, out through the passenger fender (the OEM engine-room main's only bay crossing - EA1/EB1/EB2) to the MR-S EHPS pump (vacated ABS actuator space), the alternator, and the passenger headlight; A/C compressor clutch stays on engine harness A/B, not drawn here. Then across the front of the bay: horn (R/B5 fallback, see n_probe), both uprated fans (core-support run). Then down the driver side - where J/B No.2 actually sits - to the driver headlight and the J/B No.2 dummy header (oem_jb2_2a/2d/2e: HL/HR/HZ/DOME/RTR) and wiper-park feed (gbx_body c9, not yet wired - no sourced wiper-motor circuit to draw against). Ends at driver J/B No.1 and R/B No.2, left kick (IE1 AM1/AM2, J/B1 primary B+, R/B2 POWER fuse in). A BLUE cabin run also crosses from the driver kick back to the passenger PDB, and a BLUE run rides alongside RED out to the trunk. Crash sensors and ABS solenoid are deleted - do not refeed 60A FL ABS, A7/A8, A11/A12, A37.",
      "color": "Green",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 390
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shdr_0",
      "text": "TRUNK + GLOVE BOX",
      "color": "Green",
      "width": 270,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 570
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shdr_1",
      "text": "FIREWALL RADLOK",
      "color": "Orange",
      "width": 270,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 660
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_probe",
      "text": "PROBE BEFORE CRIMPING 2E-2 / 2E-3. Starting + ignition (EWD p.48) puts AM1 on 2E-2/2E-5 and AM2 on 2E-3/2E-6, then IE1-10 / IE1-17. Inner circuit (p.21) puts 30A RTR on 2E-2 and 15A HAZ-HORN on 2E-3. If the unplugged 2E-2 shows continuity to IE1-10, that pin is AM1 - do not land the RTR fuse (gbx_body c8) there. Same for 2E-3 vs IE1-17 / AM2. HEAD 2A-3/2A-6 and DOME 2E-4 do not sit on that pass-through. Horn fallback is R/B5.",
      "color": "Red",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 750
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shdr_2",
      "text": "OEM INJECTION (keep J/Bs)",
      "color": "Red",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 960
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shdr_3",
      "text": "NEW ENGINE-ROOM LOADS - MR-S EHPS pump (one device: relay + 3 connectors) and both uprated fans",
      "color": "Blue",
      "width": 270,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 1050
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note_acamp",
      "text": "A/C IS THE AMPLIFIERS' BUSINESS, NOT THE ECU'S OR THE CSB3'S - and there are TWO\nRead off the factory EWD automatic-A/C pages, saved in ewd-snips:\n  p150  AUTO A/C AMPLIFIER  A32=conn A, A33=conn B, A34=conn C\n        A1 Ambient Temp -> TAM, conn C pin 6, Y-B (via EA1 4, IQ1 1)\n        A27 Water Temp  -> TW,  conn C pin 20, R-G\n  p152  A/C AMPLIFIER A18 - a SEPARATE module\n        A5 Pressure SW  -> A18 pin 13, Y-R (via EB2 2, E10, IJ1 15)\nAmbient sensor -> amplifier and pressure switch -> A18 stay FACTORY wiring\n(harness redesign 2026-09-27); this loom does not redraw them.\nNew here: only the ACPS +12V feed, a flying lead into A5 pin 1 (V-R).\nThe amplifier's own coolant switch comes from Engine-A via bulkhead A\nc37/c38 and IX_AC_CTS (ST185-ACAmp-Spur). The ECU's only A/C tie is\nAux 4 / A18 ACT kill, a flying lead on ST185-A-cabin.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 1170
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nGlove-box body block (fuses +  IGN: Ignition-switched relay coil feed (not yet wired)\nGlove-box body block (fuses +  HL: HEAD LH - relay 87, 15 A fuse -> J/B2 2A-3 / 2D-2\nGlove-box body block (fuses +  HR: HEAD RH - relay 87, 15 A fuse -> J/B2 2A-6 / 2D-6\nGlove-box body block (fuses +  WP: Wiper park - relay 87, 15 A fuse (optional, unused)\nGlove-box body block (fuses +  CSB: CSB3 permanent feed, 5 A - stays live for the kill sequence (plan 6.48)\nGlove-box body block (fuses +  DEV: Cluster + RealDash Pi - ignition-switched fuse only, on and off with the car; no hold relay (Daniel 2026-09-28)\nGlove-box body block (fuses +  ACPS: A/C pressure switch +12V, 5 A fuse, ignition-switched (was wrongly on F7 60A, the EPS pump fuse)\nCondenser fan relay (uprated, diode) 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - Ign 5 / B13, diode-suppressed relay fitted (TE 7-1904094-9)\nOEM J/B2 2A (engine room main) 2: 30A CDS FAN out - DO NOT REFEED, fan moved to k_fan2\nOEM J/B2 2A (engine room main) 5: Engine main relay 87 - DO NOT REFEED, Link EFI in Power\nOEM J/B2 2D (engine room main) 3: Headlight relay coil - unused, PMU switches the lamps\nOEM J/B2 2E (engine room main) 2: PROBE: inner cct = 30A RTR; starting p.48 = AM1 with 2E-5\nOEM J/B2 2E (engine room main) 3: PROBE: inner cct = 15A HAZ-HORN; starting p.48 = AM2 with 2E-6\nOEM J/B2 2E (engine room main) 4: 20A DOME (inner circuit, not on AM1/AM2 path) - PMU O4\nOEM J/B2 2E (engine room main) 5: AM1 pass-through (starting p.48). Do not PMU-feed. Restored at IE1-10\nOEM J/B2 2E (engine room main) 6: AM2 / engine-main related. Do not PMU-feed. Restored at IE1-17\nOEM R/B4 (right kick, by glove STR: OEM starter relay - isolate, Link k_str replaces\nMR-S EHPS pump (A power / B si A-1: [A 90980-12068 pin 1] +12V from k_eps 87 (glove box, ST185-B-cabin), passenger fender; 8 AWG (sized 2026-09-28 against the AMI-60 - sot/channels.csv k_eps c1)\nMR-S EHPS pump (A power / B si A-2: [A 90980-12068 pin 2] GND, 8 AWG to engine block / EB\nMR-S EHPS pump (A power / B si B-2: [B 90980-10897 pin 2] SPD Out - speed-pulse output to ECU-A A27\nMR-S EHPS pump (A power / B si B-6: [B 90980-10897 pin 6] relay request out - NOT WIRED. 6.16 moved the EPS relay trigger to the ECU (Ign 6 / ecu_b B12). Kept for reference.\nMR-S EHPS pump (A power / B si C-1: [C 90980-10942 pin 1] IG-switched, F13 7.5A - pump enable\nA/C Ambient Temp Sensor (EWD A 1: Ambient temp signal -> A/C amplifier. Thermistor, 2-wire. NOT an ECU input - the ECU has no use for outside air temp.\nA/C Ambient Temp Sensor (EWD A 2: Ambient temp sensor return -> A/C amplifier. The amp supplies its own sensor ground; do NOT tie this to chassis or to Gnd Out.\namb_temp (label): A/C Ambient Temp Sensor (EWD A1, behind front bumper)\nA/C Pressure Switch (EWD A5) - 1: +12V in, wire V-R. EWD p152. Fed from the glove-box body block APS, 5 A.\nA/C Pressure Switch (EWD A5) - 4: Switched out -> A/C AMPLIFIER A18 pin 13, wire Y-R. EWD p152.\nAUTO A/C AMPLIFIER A34 = conn  C-6: TAM - ambient temp in. EWD p150: A1 pin 2 -> EA1 4 -> IQ1 1 -> TAM, conn C pin 6, wire Y-B.\nA/C AMPLIFIER A18 (separate mo 13: A/C pressure switch in. EWD p152: A5 pin 4 -> EB2 2 -> E10 -> IJ1 15 -> A18 pin 13, wire Y-R. Shares this net with the A3 A/C idle-up VSV.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 1920
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_jb_disposition",
      "text": "J/B AND RELAY BLOCK DISPOSITION - owned by docs/electrical/ENGINE-ROOM-POWER-REDISTRIBUTION.md: §4 method, §5.2 J/B No.1 + R/B No.2 (left kick), §5.3 R/B No.3 / No.4 (right kick), §5.4 vacated J/B No.2 cavities, §5.6 deleted circuits, §8 glove-box fuse schedule. Read it there - this drawing does not repeat it.",
      "color": "Red",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3660,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_rb2_rb3",
      "text": "R/B No.2 (LEFT KICK) / R/B No.3 (RIGHT KICK) - EWD p.23, docs/electrical/ewd-snips/1990-st185-rb2-left-rb3-right.png (1990 book - confirm on the 1993 car). R/B No.2: Power Main Relay (4-pin) + 30A POWER fuse (housing pins 1-2). Loom C feeds the fuse input from the PDB (w_rb2 -> oem_rb2 c1); the relay stays in circuit (oem_rb2 c2). R/B No.3: Fog Light Relay (4-pin) only; not drawn here - keep only if fog lights stay. Actions: power doc §5.2 L9, §5.3 R4.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3660,
        "y": 240
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_alt_prot",
      "text": "ALTERNATOR OUTPUT PROTECTION (Daniel 2026-09-28): a fusible link or an inline fuse / breaker on the positive cable at the trunk battery or near the cabin fuse box / PDB - never at the starter post. Size for the 160 A alternator (plan 6.20: 175 A). Battery is AGM. The trunk Longacre 4-terminal kill switch cuts the battery positive and, on its second pair, the alternator IG feed.",
      "color": "Orange",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1080,
        "y": 690
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_jb2_side",
      "text": "J/B No.2 SIDE + FENDER ROUTING DECISION (2026-09-29). ENGINE-ROOM-POWER-REDISTRIBUTION.md previously said J/B No.2 was passenger-side; that was backwards (corrected the same day - see that doc's own cross-check, EWD p.16 vs p.24). J/B No.2 is on the DRIVER side. This drawing's dummy-header wires (w_pmu_hl/hr/horn/dome/rtr, feeding oem_jb2_2a/2d/2e) were themselves modelled assuming the old passenger-side location; they do NOT actually ride the passenger ABS trough alongside the EPS pump - only the EPS pump, alternator and passenger headlight stay on that passenger run. Fender routing (Daniel gave a preferred path, flexible if a shorter run existed): starting passenger (matching the PDB and the OEM's own only fender crossing) and finishing driver-side at J/B No.2 and J/B No.1 is shorter than the reverse, which would need a crossing before AND after the passenger-side loads. Kept as given. Exact bundle lengths on the oem_jb2_2a/2d/2e branches (currently 1.3-1.4 m) are pre-existing estimates, not re-measured against this correction - verify on the car before cutting cable.",
      "color": "Red",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 450
      }
    }
  ]
}
